### Problem Description

You are given an $M \times N$ grid (matrix) representing a box that contains several stones, where empty spaces are represented by dots (`.`) and stones are represented by stars (`*`).

The simulation involves the following sequence of operations:

1. **Initial Gravity:** Apply gravity so that all stones fall down to the bottom of their respective columns (filling empty spaces from the bottom up).
2. **Rotation:** Rotate the entire grid by $90^\circ$ either **left** (anticlockwise) or **right** (clockwise) based on a given direction command.
3. **Final Gravity:** Apply gravity again to the rotated grid so that all stones settle down to the bottom of their new columns.

The objective is to output the final state of the grid after completing all these steps.

---

### Constraints

* Number of rows ($M$) $\ge 3$ [[09:36](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tEzttXAYpoM&t=576)]
* Number of columns ($N$) $\le 200$ [[09:36](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tEzttXAYpoM&t=576)]
* Grid characters: `.` represents empty spaces, and `*` represents stones [[09:49](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tEzttXAYpoM&t=589)].
* Direction input string: `"left"` or `"right"` [[20:31](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tEzttXAYpoM&t=1231)].

---

### Input

* The first line contains two space-separated integers, $M$ and $N$, representing the number of rows and columns [[17:40](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tEzttXAYpoM&t=1060)].
* The next $M$ lines each contain a string or character sequence of length $N$ representing the initial state of the grid rows [[18:19](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tEzttXAYpoM&t=1099)].
* The final line contains a string indicating the rotation direction (`left` or `right`) [[20:31](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tEzttXAYpoM&t=1231)].

---

### Output

* The resulting $M \times N$ grid (matrix) printed row by row after applying the initial gravity, rotation, and final gravity steps [[24:03](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tEzttXAYpoM&t=1443)].

---

### Example

#### Sample Input

```text
4 4
..**
.*.*
***.
.*..
right

```

#### Explanation / Steps

1. **Initial Grid Setup:** A $4 \times 4$ matrix with stones (`*`) placed at specified coordinates.
2. **Apply Initial Gravity:** Stones fall down to the lowest available rows in each column.
3. **Rotation:** Rotate the grid $90^\circ$ clockwise (`right`) [[12:59](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tEzttXAYpoM&t=779)].
4. **Apply Final Gravity:** Stones settle down again to the bottom of the columns in the newly rotated grid [[14:13](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tEzttXAYpoM&t=853)].

